# Vendored competitor sources, kept locally for research.
#
# The clones are disposable — `_refsrc/README.md` says so, and the analysis in
# `docs/RESEARCH-AND-PLAN.md` cites files and line numbers rather than depending on the tree.
# But that README is the one part that is not reproducible: it records the exact commit each
# repository was cloned at, which is what every claim in the research log is a claim *about*.
# Ignored along with everything else, it lived only on one machine.
#
# `_refsrc/*` rather than `_refsrc/`, because git does not descend into an excluded directory
# and a negation inside one never matches.
_refsrc/*
!_refsrc/README.md

